{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And I will harden the heart of Pharaoh, and he will pursue after them</b> — Since Pharaoh feared them because of the plague of the firstborn and sought from them, \"and bless me also\" (Exodus 12:32), he had no intention of pursuing after them even if they fled; rather, he was content to let Moses do with them as he pleased. Therefore it was necessary to say that He Himself would strengthen his heart to pursue after them. And further below (Exodus 14:17) He said a second time, \"Behold, I will harden the heart of Egypt, and they shall come after them\" — for when they saw that the sea split before Israel and they were walking on dry ground within it, how could their hearts summon the courage to enter after them to do them harm? There is nothing in all the wonders like this marvel, and this was truly madness for them; but He dulled their counsel and strengthened their hearts to enter into the sea:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:07:32.250267835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}